        "original_id": "a6e08e97-6f88-5510-a39d-919e5e0c5153",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: California\n- People: Indigenous Americans\n- Events: Compromise of 1850, Mexican–American War\n- Organizations: United States Congress\n- Topics: California history before 1900, U.S. statehood\n\nFacts:\n- Indigenous Americans first arrived in California about 13,000 to 15,000 years ago, marking the beginning of human history in California.\n- The Mexican–American War took place from 1846 to 1848.\n- In September 1850, the United States Congress passed the Compromise of 1850 as a package of five separate bills.\n- The Compromise of 1850 defused a four-year political confrontation between slave states and free states over the status of territories acquired during the Mexican–American War.\n- In 1850, California joined the Union as a free state because of the Compromise of 1850.",
